 ],
 "asserts": "MQSABKO holds one MQBACK call_sites fact (form literal, resolves_to null, a gaps entry), called from 0000-MAIN, and no SRRCMIT / SRRBACK / MQCMIT call. Step LKBKO20 of MQSALNK is a jcl_steps fact (program IEWL) whose SYSLIN instream data yields jcl_utility_cards facts INCLUDE SYSLIB(CSQBSTUB), INCLUDE OBJLIB(MQSABKO) and NAME MQSABKO(R): it is linked with CSQBSTUB, not CSQBRSTB. The unit of work touches only MQ resources, which is the case IBM gives for MQBACK in a batch program. Contrast H-0111, where the back-out is SRRBACK because the program is linked with the RRS stub.",
